 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.8 (unreleased)
+
+Issues #766, #767, #768, #680, #676, #375 (rest), #404 (wake part), #405 (install part), #377 (response helpers and test). Written without compiling or running the build tool; the main chat builds and runs the tests. All additions; nothing breaks.
+
+- Added (#766): `fail_limit` is public and `FailLimiter` is re-exported at the crate root. Keys are `u64` ids (a connection id, or a hash of a peer address), so an app can drop its own copy. Same limits as the host uses.
+- Added (#767): `supervisor::supervise_with(config, SuperviseOptions, launch, probe, on_event)`. `SuperviseOptions::adopt(child)` supervises a child the caller already started and verified as generation 1 (`launch` is first called only when it is gone and the policy restarts it); `SupervisorMode` (a shared number) with `SuperviseOptions::mode`, `SupervisorHandle::mode` and `restart_with_mode(value)` lets a restart start the child in another state, such as a locked launch; `SupervisorHandle::stop_returning_child` ends the supervisor and returns the running child alive (stdin open, nothing killed) for an ordered shutdown. `supervise` is `supervise_with` with the default options.
+- Added (#768): `Client::call_retrying_pooled` and `call_retrying_pooled_until`: the connect closure returns anything that `Borrow<Client>` (an `Arc<Client>` from a pool, a lease guard), so a pooled connection is not dropped after each attempt. `Client::is_closed` tells a pool to discard a connection. `call_retrying_over` and `call_retrying_until` are unchanged.
+- Added (#680): `current_user_sid_string()` is public on Windows (it was crate-private), re-exported at the crate root. The `rightkit-child-process` half of #680 (stdin on output/status) belongs to that crate.
+- Fixed (#676): on Windows `Suite::private_service_subdir`, `data_dir` and every other private directory the crate makes now get the protected owner-only DACL of `rightkit_fs::restrict_owner_only`, so `rightkit_fs::private::is_owner_only` is true for them. Failing to harden is an error (`SuiteError::Insecure`), not an open directory. Unix is unchanged.
+- Added (#375): `stop::stop_on_parent_exit(source, pid)` (polls every 200 ms; compares the OS start marker so a recycled pid is not taken for the parent; cause `Requested`, so `StopCause` is unchanged), `stop::parent_pid()` (Unix `getppid`) and `stop::at_exit(hook)` (C `atexit`; runs last-registered first on a normal exit, panics contained). The signal and stdin parts were in 0.2.7.
+- Added (#404, wake part): module `wake` (`Wake`, `WakeListener`, `WakeError`): Darwin notification on macOS, a named auto-reset event with the owner-only DACL on Windows, a polled counter file in the suite's private `wake` directory elsewhere. A hint without data; posts coalesce. Not built: publish/subscribe events (`events.subscribe`), `ServiceRecord` heartbeat/state fields and the attach-or-fallback client (they change the record schema and the app contract), and the RightKitSwift observer.
+- Added (#405, install part): module `install` (`ServiceSpec`, `ServiceManager`, `SystemdUser`, `LaunchAgent`, `ScheduledTask`, `CommandRunner`, `SystemRunner`, `platform_manager`, pure `render_systemd_unit`, `render_launch_agent_plist`, `render_task_xml`, `windows_quote_arg`). Not built: Windows services (SCM) and a public `verify_authenticode`.
+- Added (#377): `Response::json`, `Response::redirect` and `Response::with_header` so a public-route handler can build its answer, and a test of the public-route path (`tests/remote_daemon.rs`). `Daemon::add_public_route` itself shipped in 0.2.7.
+- Not built: #379 (browser bearer-token device auth), #666 (reload saga). See the report for the reasons.
+
 ## 0.2.7 (2026-10-17)
 
 Issues #375, #376, #384, #453 (listener part), #504, #596, #377 (public routes). Written without compiling or running the build tool here; CI builds and runs the tests. The crate version is unchanged.
